134
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:43,780
it run down the sides.
沿着柱壁流下去。

135
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:48,940
Continuing, we can see that our mixture is starting to separate into individual components.
继续下去，我们可以看到混合物开始分离成单独的组分。

136
00:08:48,940 --> 00:08:54,260
Again, since we have colored chemicals, it will be easier to observe the separation.
同样，由于我们用的是有颜色的化学物质，分离会更容易观察。

137
00:08:54,260 --> 00:08:58,960
The dark green mixture we started with is separating into blue and yellow colors.
我们一开始的深绿色混合物正在分成蓝色和黄色。

138
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:01,520
This is why we have to collect fractions.
这就是为什么我们必须分段收集馏分。

139
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:06,320
If we just collect these in one container, they will mix together again.
如果我们把它们都收集在一个容器里，它们又会重新混在一起。

140
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:10,260
This way we isolate the components in separate fractions.
这样我们就把各组分分离到了不同的馏分中。

141
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:14,720
At first you will be collecting only solvent, but as you can see, the yellow band is getting
一开始你收集到的只有溶剂，但如你所见，黄色色带越来越

142
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:16,480
closer to the bottom.
接近底部了。

143
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:21,860
Keep adding the eluent and collecting fractions until you have collected all your compounds.
继续加洗脱剂并收集馏分，直到收集到所有化合物为止。

144
00:09:21,860 --> 00:09:26,460
When the compounds are not visible, you will have to perform TLC to find out what's
当化合物看不见时，你就必须做 TLC，来确定

145
00:09:26,460 --> 00:09:27,700
in each fraction.
每个馏分里有什么。

146
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:32,320
You can test many fractions on one plate, and all the fractions that show data for
你可以在一块板上检测许多馏分，所有显示含有

147
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:37,780
a particular compound can be combined and the solvent evaporated, to give you a pure
某一化合物的馏分都可以合并，再蒸发掉溶剂，就能得到纯净的

148
00:09:37,780 --> 00:09:39,520
isolated product.
分离产物。

149
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:44,020
If you know for sure which compound you want, you can dispose of the rest, but sometimes
如果你确定自己想要哪种化合物，就可以把其余的处理掉，但有时

150
00:09:44,020 --> 00:09:47,200
you will want to isolate two or more products.
你会想要分离出两种或更多产物。

151
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:52,140
There are times where, rather than TLC, you will want to analyze the fractions by absorbance
有时候，你会不用 TLC，而是用吸收

152
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:59,120
spectroscopy, UV, or a colorimetric assay to figure out the identities of any compounds.
光谱、紫外或比色法来分析馏分，以确定各化合物的身份。

153
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:05,600
But in this particular case we were able to isolate these compounds using just our eyes.
但在这个例子中，我们只用肉眼就能分离出这些化合物。

154
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:08,900
Column chromatography can get much more complex than this.
柱色谱可以比这复杂得多。

155
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:14,000
In several forms of chromatography, we use more than one solvent system, either in succession
在好几种色谱方法中，我们会使用不止一种溶剂体系，要么依次使用，

156
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:19,700
or applied as a gradient, usually increasing in polarity over time to push out substances
要么以梯度方式施加，通常极性随时间逐渐增大，以便把

157
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:21,420
that traveled more slowly.
移动较慢的物质推出来。

158
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:27,380
Furthermore, the material in the column can be agarose, acrylamide, or some other compound
此外，色谱柱中的材料可以是琼脂糖、丙烯酰胺或其他化合物，

159
00:10:27,380 --> 00:10:29,460
depending on what we're separating.
这取决于我们要分离的是什么。

160
00:10:29,460 --> 00:10:35,060
In the lab we can use columns to separate things such as peptides or drugs based on
在实验室里，我们可以用色谱柱根据大小、电荷、极性或其他亲和性等方面

161
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:40,260
aspects such as size, charge, polarity, or other affinities.
来分离多肽或药物之类的物质。

162
00:10:40,260 --> 00:10:45,700
The packing, mixing, and collection of these can also be automated in large-scale academic
在大规模的学术和工业流程中，这些柱子的装填、混合和收集也可以

163
00:10:45,700 --> 00:10:47,700
and industrial processes.
实现自动化。

164
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:54,660
A sophisticated example of column chromatography is FPLC, or fast protein liquid chromatography,
柱色谱的一个复杂例子是 FPLC，即快速蛋白液相色谱，

165
00:10:54,660 --> 00:10:57,740
a technique that is used to separate proteins.
这是一种用于分离蛋白质的技术。

166
00:10:57,740 --> 00:11:13,650
But for now, that concludes an introduction to column chromatography.
不过现在，柱色谱的入门介绍就到此结束。
